    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling output today, headlined by **Yordan Alvarez** (75.69) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.53). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our most reliable anchor against Leiter, benefiting from an elite .421 xwOBA that transcends park factors. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our primary strategic play for stolen bases; he faces a favorable matchup against a pitcher with a slow delivery (87% SB success rate), and his score is bolstered by a strong platoon advantage that makes him a priority start despite hitting in the bottom third of the order. **Junior Caminero** (67.27) also grades out as a top-tier play, leveraging his elevated spot in the order and a favorable matchup against Junk to provide balanced production across our scoring categories.\n\nOur lineup construction process required a difficult choice regarding the bench, with **Carson Benge** (46.30) narrowly missing the cut. While **Carson Benge** maintains a solid floor, the optimizer prioritized the higher projected efficiency and specific situational utility\u2014such as the stolen base potential offered by **Hyeseong Kim**\u2014found in our starting nine. We remain cautious regarding **Trea Turner** (53.83) and **Kyle Schwarber** (52.46), as both are facing the challenge of Ashcraft, whose respectable 3.52 xERA suppresses their raw output. We are also monitoring the status of **Casey Schmitt** (63.20); his start is contingent on his assumed #3 spot in the lineup, and while he carries a strong projection, his utility as an elite defensive catcher adds a slight drag to his offensive scoring efficiency. Keep a close watch on these assignments, as any shift in the batting order for **Casey Schmitt** could necessitate a recalibration of his role to preserve our limited game caps.",
